From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 18:45:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: denali: preserve ath12k rfkill quirk

The WCN7850 firmware reaches mission mode but does not register a
wireless PHY when ath12k configures its firmware rfkill input on
Denali. Bluetooth is unaffected because it uses a separate UART
transport.

Restore the board property consumed by the Dale Whinham devicetree
rfkill support and record the dependency in the provenance document.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
---
 .../driver-api/media/sp11-camera-provenance.rst          | 9 +++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi        | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/driver-api/media/sp11-camera-provenance.rst b/Documentation/driver-api/media/sp11-camera-provenance.rst
index 64fb9346e4fc..a71858c5705e 100644
--- a/Documentation/driver-api/media/sp11-camera-provenance.rst
+++ b/Documentation/driver-api/media/sp11-camera-provenance.rst
@@ -60,6 +60,15 @@ CAMSS and devicetree foundations
   description uses hardware enumeration, standard firmware descriptions, and
   observations made on the author's Surface Pro 11.
 
+Denali ath12k rfkill prerequisite
+  The ath12k devicetree ``disable-rfkill`` support is Dale Whinham's GPL
+  contribution, originally commit
+  ``d7e0b837ef4672f294af3d7f59eefe7a241371db`` with his authorship and
+  Signed-off-by trailer preserved.  The matching Denali property was
+  reintroduced after a one-shot hardware test showed that WCN7850 firmware
+  initialized but no wireless PHY registered without the quirk.  Bluetooth
+  continued to operate over its separate UART transport.
+
 Review policy
 -------------
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
index ce7d958ca687..9cf8e1a5e0bf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi
@@ -950,6 +950,9 @@ wifi@0 {
 		compatible = "pci17cb,1107";
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 
+		/* Denali does not expose a usable firmware rfkill input. */
+		disable-rfkill;
+
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p59>;
 		vddwlcx-supply = <&vreg_pmu_wlcx_0p8>;
 		vddwlmx-supply = <&vreg_pmu_wlmx_0p85>;
